            "review_title": "Review at Mệ Vui Quán",
            "review_text": "Phuong Vo\n2 contributions\n0\nAverage food. Bad customer service.\nNov 2021 • Solo\nI went there for dinner and odered My Quang noodle. The place looked nice & spacious with Hoian Town vibe. The food was average, you could easily find the same food with better price in town. \nHowever, the service is terrible, it deserves 2/10, nobody seemed welcoming since the firs moment I walked in, like something really bothered them so much to have customers around. The female seemed upset and neglected when I asked them about the ingredients ( I just wanted to make sure it’s the central food taste as it’s named). All staffs walked around tiredly with their loud flipflop sound on the floor without any eyes contact with customers when they’re talking to. \nThe security even stared at me while I was having my dinner, as if my uncomfortable experience was not enough. \n\nOverall, I had a bad experience at this restaurant, which was supposed to be nice by it looked. And I wouldn’t recommend this to any other customers. I wish I had read other people’s reviews before I tried them. \n\nWhile many restaurants struggle to get back to their business, and get customers in this pandemic, this place is a joke.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 11, 2021",
